# OncoHarness

The harness lane of the Oncoscope project: a **gated, self-improving LLM harness**
that orchestrates vision models for cancer detection — designed to get measurably
better every cycle **without fooling itself**.

> **Not a medical device.** Research software only. No output of this system may
> be used for diagnosis, screening, or treatment decisions.

Extracted from [siennakc/cancer-vm](https://github.com/siennakc/cancer-vm)
(`oncoscope.harness` + gate machinery, commit `4ce701d`). The model/data lane —
real mammography ingestion, trained encoders, sealed internal test, external
MIAS benchmark — stays in cancer-vm and plugs in behind this repo's protocols.

## Architecture

A **deterministic state machine** (`ingest → preflight QC → detect → TTA verify →
zoom re-verify → FP/FN hunt → aggregate → adjudicate → conformal deferral →
report`) drives every case. Specialist **detectors propose** at high sensitivity;
the **LLM adjudicates at exactly one node** — it plans, weighs verified evidence,
and decides recall / no-recall / defer, but it **never sees pixels and never
authors a number**. Images live in a handle-passing **artifact store**; every tool
call and claim lands in an append-only, hash-chained **evidence ledger**; every
promotion must pass a conjunctive **eval gate** whose rules live in a path the
harness cannot write (CI carries an immutability canary over `gates/`).

## Layout

| module | contents |
|---|---|
| `state_machine.py` | the outer loop; LLM only at the adjudication node |
| `tools.py` | the toolbelt (detect, crop, measure, compare, gate, …) — deny-by-default allowlist |
| `ledger.py` / `store.py` | hash-chained evidence ledger; handle-passing artifact store |
| `agent.py` | Claude Agent SDK adjudicator (in-process MCP, built-ins stripped) |
| `gate.py` + `gates/` | conjunctive PASS/FAIL promotion gate; protected rules |
| `conformal.py` | Mondrian conformal deferral |
| `ablation.py` | harness-vs-detector-alone A/B runner |
| `splits.py` / `leakage.py` | patient-grouped splits + leakage audit (axiom A9) |
| `reference/` | pure-numpy reference detector/encoder/head for tests & protocols |
| `phantom.py` | synthetic phantom generator — full test suite runs with no data, no GPU |

Design axioms and the full technique catalog: [TASKSHEET.md](TASKSHEET.md).
Threat model and PHI boundary: [THREAT_MODEL.md](THREAT_MODEL.md).

## Quickstart

```sh
python3.12 -m venv .venv
.venv/bin/pip install -e '.[dev]'
.venv/bin/python -m pytest        # 27 tests, seconds, no data, no GPU
```

Run the pipeline on a synthetic phantom:

```sh
.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'
from oncoharness.phantom import generate_dataset
from oncoharness.ledger import EvidenceLedger
from oncoharness.state_machine import HarnessPipeline
from oncoharness.store import ArtifactStore
from oncoharness.tools import Toolbelt

case = next(c for c in generate_dataset() if c.label == 1)
pipeline = HarnessPipeline(Toolbelt(ArtifactStore("runs/demo/artifacts"),
                                    EvidenceLedger("runs/demo/ledger.jsonl")))
print(pipeline.run_case(case.case_id, case.pixels).model_dump_json(indent=1))
PY
```

## Non-negotiables

- The LLM never authors pixels, coordinates, or numbers (A3).
- Generator and checker are independent; verification is symmetric (A4, A5).
- Abstention is a first-class output; deferral ships evidence (A13).
- The harness can never write its own gates — **self-improving, never
  self-certifying**.
